act = {"start": "2026-11-14 13:15", "end": "2026-11-14 14:44", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 11", "act": "Mārama", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/marama-jchy", "blurb": "A young Māori woman faces the horror of her colonial heritage in this stunning Gothic horror.\nMary leaves New Zealand for Victorian Yorkshire looking to explore her family history. Against her better judgement, she takes on a role as governess in Hawkser Manor. But something is off and Mary realises she may be trapped inside the estate with buried secrets and dark, terrifying visions. A brooding and poignant exploration of the horror of colonialism and the erasing of Māori culture.\nContains strong injury detail, violence, threat, disturbing scenes."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-14 12:45", "end": "2026-11-14 14:25", "stage": "Cottage Road Cinema", "act": "The History of Concrete", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/the-history-of-concrete-53rn", "blurb": "After attending a Hallmark movie workshop, John Wilson turns his new knowledge to a film about concrete, delivered with his usual dry wit.\nFinding himself with too much time on his hands, Wilson wonders if he can apply the winning rom-com formula to a documentary about the dullest thing. From a man removing chewing gum from pavements to runners circling the same flat block, to dinner with Kim Kardashian, his feature debut proves again that Wilson is a master at finding absurd hilarity in the mundane.\nContains ableist attitudes and language."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-14 13:00", "end": "2026-11-14 14:59", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 7", "act": "Taipei Story", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/taipei-story-fvmq", "blurb": "Edward Yang’s melancholy masterpiece captures Taipei at a moment of dizzying transformation.\nAs ambitious Chin looks towards the future, her boyfriend Lung, played by fellow New Taiwan Cinema master Hou Hsiao-hsien, remains tethered to the past, and their relationship begins to drift apart. Against a cityscape of gleaming towers and neon-lit streets, Yang’s gorgeous compositions capture the pace of urban change while finding moments of intimacy and beauty within the modern metropolis.\nContains scenes of violence."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-14 11:00", "end": "2026-11-14 12:47", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 11", "act": "Black Church Bay", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/black-church-bay-5zsn", "blurb": "Acclaimed for his short films - Pale Saint screened in the British short film competition at LIFF 2019 - writer-director Rhys Marc Jones has made a striking debut feature with Black Church Bay, a gripping and thought-provoking mystery thriller.\nIn a Welsh fishing village, deputy head teacher Barry (Tom Cullen) starts an affair with one of his students Jasper (Joe Locke). One night, Jasper mysteriously disappears, and Barry’s closely guarded secret threatens to come to light.\nThe screening on 13 November 2026 will be followed by a Q&A with Director Rhys Marc Jones.\nContains scenes with nudity and sex."}
